  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "With German gone and Claude Monet once again without a head chef, owner Dmitry Nagiyev gathers the entire staff in the dining room. Instead of simply rehiring Viktor Petrovich, Nagiyev announces that the restaurant will host a nationwide television cooking show. Let's listen to his dramatic pitch in Russian.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Повара сойдутся в честной борьбе.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Смотрите главное кулинарное шоу страны.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Главный приз — один миллион рублей.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "И место шеф-повара лучшего ресторана.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Хозяином этого ресторана являюсь я.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Меня зовут Дмитрий Нагиев.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Желаю всем приятного аппетита.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Чего мы так тихо молчим?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Наш корабль остался без капитана.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Меня ночью посетила отличная мысль.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Мы организуем популярное телевизионное шоу.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "И нового шефа тоже найдём.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Now let's break down the details of Nagiyev's television show announcement line by line.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Повара сойдутся в честной борьбе.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'The cooks will meet in a fair fight.' A reflexive third-person plural future verb of coming together takes a prepositional phrase.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Смотрите главное кулинарное шоу страны.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Watch the main culinary show of the country.' A plural imperative invites viewers to watch, followed by an indeclinable neuter noun and genitive modifier.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Главный приз — один миллион рублей.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'The grand prize is one million rubles.' The masculine numeral phrase meaning one million governs the genitive plural of rubles.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "И место шеф-повара лучшего ресторана.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And the head chef spot at the best restaurant.' A superlative genitive singular phrase modifies the noun for restaurant.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Хозяином этого ресторана являюсь я.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'The owner of this restaurant is me.' The formal reflexive verb meaning to be or serve as requires the instrumental singular on the noun for owner.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Меня зовут Дмитрий Нагиев.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'My name is Dmitry Nagiyev.' Nagiyev introduces himself using the standard third-person plural naming construction.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Желаю всем приятного аппетита.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I wish everyone bon appetit.' The traditional mealtime wish stands in the genitive singular after a verb of wishing.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Чего мы так тихо молчим?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Why are we keeping so quiet?' Snapping out of his daydream, Nagiyev asks the silent staff why nobody is applauding.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Наш корабль остался без капитана.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Our ship has been left without a captain.' The preposition meaning without governs the animate genitive singular of the noun for captain.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Меня ночью посетила отличная мысль.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'A great thought came to me in the night.' A feminine past verb agrees with the feminine nominative singular noun meaning thought.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Мы организуем популярное телевизионное шоу.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'We will organize a popular television show.' Two neuter singular adjectives modify the indeclinable loanword meaning show.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "И нового шефа тоже найдём.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And we will find a new head chef too.' The animate accusative singular of head chef takes a genitive-like ending. Let's hear Nagiyev's entire pitch in Russian from start to finish.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
